  ### Test Case Suite: BUG-1024 (Checkout Discount Coupon Failure)                                                                
                                                                                                                                  
  As a Senior QA Test Case Engineer, I have analyzed the bug report (BUG-1024) where applying a valid discount coupon causes a    
  `500 Internal Server Error` during the "Place Order" action in the Checkout / Payment module.                                   
                                                                                                                                  
  Below is the comprehensive, structured, and executable test case suite covering functional, positive, negative, boundary        
  conditions, edge cases, input validation, business rules, error handling, and regression scenarios to ensure the bug is fixed   
  and no side effects are introduced.                                                                                             
                                                                                                                                  
  ---                                                                                                                             
                                                                                                                                  
  ### Test Case Matrix                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                  
  | Test Case ID | Requirement Reference | Title | Preconditions | Test Data | Test Steps | Expected Result | Test Type |         
  Priority | Coverage Classification |                                                                                            
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |                                                         
  | **TC_CHK_001** | BUG-1024 | Verify successful checkout with a valid percentage discount coupon | • User is logged in<br>•     
  Cart contains eligible item(s)<br>• Valid coupon exists in DB | Coupon Code: `SAVE10` (10% off) | 1. Add item to cart.<br>2.    
  Navigate to Cart/Checkout.<br>3. Enter `SAVE10` and apply.<br>4. Proceed to payment.<br>5. Click "Place Order". | • Coupon      
  discount is applied correctly.<br>• Order is placed successfully (200 OK).<br>• Order confirmation page is displayed. |         
  Functional / Positive | High | Happy Path / Bug Fix Verification |                                                              
  | **TC_CHK_002** | BUG-1024 | Verify successful checkout with a valid fixed-amount discount coupon | • User is logged in<br>•   
  Cart total > coupon value | Coupon Code: `FLAT20` ($20 off) | 1. Add item worth $50 to cart.<br>2. Apply `FLAT20`               
  coupon.<br>3. Fill shipping/payment details.<br>4. Click "Place Order". | • Fixed discount is deducted.<br>• Order places       
  successfully without 500 error.<br>• Correct final amount is charged. | Functional / Positive | High | Business Rules |         
  | **TC_CHK_003** | BUG-1024 | Verify behavior when applying an expired discount coupon | • Coupon has expired in the system |   
  Coupon Code: `EXPIRED50` | 1. Add item to cart.<br>2. Apply `EXPIRED50` coupon.<br>3. Attempt to proceed to checkout / place    
  order. | • System rejects the coupon with a clear error message ("Coupon has expired").<br>• Order cannot be placed with this   
  coupon. | Negative | Medium | Input Validation / Business Rules |                                                               
  | **TC_CHK_004** | BUG-1024 | Verify behavior when applying a non-existent/invalid coupon code | • User is on the               
  cart/checkout page | Coupon Code: `INVALID999` | 1. Add item to cart.<br>2. Enter `INVALID999` and click Apply. | • System      
  displays an error message ("Invalid coupon code").<br>• Cart total remains unchanged. | Negative | Medium | Input Validation |  
  | **TC_CHK_005** | BUG-1024 | Verify boundary condition: Coupon applied on cart total exactly equal to minimum spend limit | •  
  Minimum spend limit for coupon is $50 | Coupon Code: `MIN50` (Min spend $50)<br>Cart Total: $50.00 | 1. Add items totaling      
  exactly $50.00 to cart.<br>2. Apply `MIN50` coupon.<br>3. Click "Place Order". | • Coupon is accepted.<br>• Checkout completes  
  successfully with the discount applied. | Boundary Condition | High | Boundary Value Analysis |                                 
  | **TC_CHK_006** | BUG-1024 | Verify edge case: Coupon applied when cart total falls just below the minimum spend limit | •     
  Minimum spend limit for coupon is $50 | Coupon Code: `MIN50`<br>Cart Total: $49.99 | 1. Add items totaling $49.99 to            
  cart.<br>2. Apply `MIN50` coupon.<br>3. Attempt checkout. | • System displays minimum spend restriction error.<br>• Discount    
  is not applied. | Edge Case | Medium | Boundary Value Analysis |                                                                
  | **TC_CHK_007** | BUG-1024 | Verify edge case: Coupon application resulting in a zero-dollar ($0.00) order total | • Free      
  item promotion or 100% discount coupon available | Coupon Code: `FREE100` (100% off) | 1. Add item worth $30 to cart.<br>2.     
  Apply `FREE100` coupon (Total becomes $0.00).<br>3. Select free payment method (if applicable) and click "Place Order". | •     
  Order is processed successfully without requiring payment gateway interaction.<br>• Order status is set to completed/paid. |    
  Edge Case | High | Special Business Rules |                                                                                     
  | **TC_CHK_008** | BUG-1024 | Verify server error handling and user feedback when backend fails during "Place Order" | •        
  Mock/Simulate backend database timeout or unexpected server exception | Valid Coupon Code: `SAVE10` | 1. Apply `SAVE10` to      
  cart.<br>2. Trigger a simulated 500 error on the backend payment endpoint.<br>3. Click "Place Order". | • System catches the    
  exception gracefully.<br>• User-friendly error message is displayed (e.g., "An unexpected error occurred. Please try again      
  later.").<br>• User is not left on a blank/loading screen. | Error Handling | High | Robustness / Resilience |                  
  | **TC_CHK_009** | BUG-1024 | Verify checkout functionality *without* any discount coupon applied (Regression) | • Clean user   
  session | N/A | 1. Add item to cart without adding any coupon.<br>2. Proceed to checkout.<br>3. Click "Place Order". | •        
  Standard checkout processes successfully.<br>• Ensures core checkout flow wasn't broken by the coupon bug fix. | Regression |   
  High | Regression / Base Functionality |                                                                                        
  | **TC_CHK_010** | BUG-1024 | Verify coupon removal functionality prior to placing order | • Coupon `SAVE10` is already         
  applied to the cart | Coupon Code: `SAVE10` | 1. Apply `SAVE10` to cart.<br>2. Click the "Remove" / "X" button next to the      
  coupon.<br>3. Proceed to checkout and click "Place Order". | • Coupon is successfully removed from cart.<br>• Cart total        
  reverts to original price.<br>• Order places successfully at original price. | Functional / Positive | Medium | State           
